; A rule of the wrong kind for its position (MAC-LANG-14). `limit`'s
; two-argument rule generates declarations and its three-argument rule
; one expression. The first rule that matches decides, so a
; three-argument invocation at the top level, and a two-argument one in
; an expression, are each `AX3027` at the invocation.
(macro limit
  ((limit name value) (:: name Int) (fn (name) value))
  ((limit lo hi x) (if (< x lo) lo (> x hi) hi x)))

(limit 0 10 42)

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (limit ceiling 10))
